  "note": "RP2040 UF2 images for every rind-bench file, built for thumbv6m-none-eabi. Timed with SysTick at 125 MHz (1 cycle resolution; 24-bit hardware extended to 32 bits). ring 0.17 left out (NEON assembly). Built, not yet run on hardware; no usable QEMU. The public repo is [steelhead99x/rind-hardware](https://github.com/steelhead99x/rind-hardware); its root `8d9c1bb` is a squash of that history. Each image now has `rind_hardware` (the public SHA when the trees match, otherwise `ancestor of 8d9c1bb5e76e5ae8eb2d481535dc63ccd6a8f5f3`) and `legacy_rind_bench` (the SHA recorded at build time). `tools/legacy-rind-bench-map.json` is the map `cargo verify` and `cargo xtask` use.",
